KG42.register("source_edge_archive-2e02c02d52ed3ec1b104abfe",{"id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E002","paper":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","rule_ref":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E002","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"bidding.demand","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e20"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","target":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","source_occurrence_id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001::V::matching.counterparties","target_occurrence_id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","source_unit_id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-M01::matching.counterparties","target_unit_id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-M01::bidding.demand","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Bilateral quantity proposals produced by the update (6a). | Buying-side quantity updates in the decentralized consensus-ADMM negotiation of (6). | Buying-side trade proposals in the decentralized P2P negotiation. | Individual buying-side bilateral proposals in the update (6a). | Requested-power updates in (6a), jointly with the agent's other bilateral proposals. | Submission of buying-side trade proposals in the decentralized P2P negotiation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e20"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"274a672add2fe5ac098d8ce20b285838b507b936c23e274b21b7a85e6fe15c0e","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-M01","source_definition":"The electrical-distance network-charge signal is intended to encourage agents to trade with their electrically closest partners. Scope: Proposed electrical-distance cost allocation in the P2P community. Condition: Network charges are proportional to the electrical distance between agents. A high zonal price is intended to discourage outside agents from trading with counterparties inside that zone. Scope: Proposed zonal cost allocation with distinct zonal unit fees. Condition: A zone has a high price. Network-charge signals can induce agents to switch from their usual partners to partners unaffected by the malfunctions while retaining the same negotiation routine. Scope: Proposed use of new unit fees to handle deteriorated network operation in the P2P market. Condition: An electric-network incident causes malfunctions affecting trading partners. The bilateral trade power from agent n to agent m must be zero when m is outside n’s partnership set. Scope: Bilateral trading partnerships in the P2P formulation. Condition: Agent m is outside agent n’s trading partnership set. Partnership sets specify possible trades and do not themselves enforce market participation. Scope: Role of partnership sets in the exogenous P2P formulation. Partnership sets could be dynamically adapted in response to congestion; this is a proposed possibility rather than an asserted implemented procedure. Scope: Discussed alternative for handling congestion through changes to partnership sets. Condition: Congestion occurs.","target_definition":"The trading partnership set restricts demand proposals: the bilateral quantity must be zero for a counterparty outside that set. Scope: Buying-side trade proposals in the decentralized P2P negotiation. Condition: When a prospective counterparty is outside the requesting agent's trading partnership set. Current bilateral trade-price signals enter the participant's optimization that updates its requested energy quantities. Scope: Buying-side quantity updates in the decentralized consensus-ADMM negotiation of (6). Condition: At each negotiation iteration. Participants update requested quantities through their own optimization (6a) and individually send the resulting trade proposals to their trading partners; the negotiation process repeats until convergence. Scope: Submission of buying-side trade proposals in the decentralized P2P negotiation. Condition: During each iteration of the negotiation process, until convergence. Requested quantities must be updated consistently with the agent's total-power bounds, with total power equal to the sum of its bilateral proposals. Scope: Requested-power updates in (6a), jointly with the agent's other bilateral proposals. Condition: At every negotiation iteration. Each prosumer's requested bilateral quantity must remain within that prosumer's power boundaries. Scope: Individual buying-side bilateral proposals in the update (6a). Condition: When the requesting agent is a prosumer. The prescribed update prohibits buying requests from generators by constraining their bilateral proposed quantities to be nonnegative. Scope: Bilateral quantity proposals produced by the update (6a). Condition: When the updating agent is a generator.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"The trading partnership set restricts demand proposals: the bilateral quantity must be zero for a counterparty outside that set. Scope: Buying-side trade proposals in the decentralized P2P negotiation. Condition: When a prospective counterparty is outside the requesting agent's trading partnership set.","expression":"\\forall n,\\ \\forall m:\\ m\\notin\\omega_n\\Rightarrow p_{nm}=0","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["p_nm"],"parameter_refs":["omega_n"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e20"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e09","location":{"location_id":"src-12e1fd7a17-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. P2P Market Design","anchor_text":"⎜ ⎟ t (2) P = ⎝ ... ... ... ⎠ wo pNΩ 1 · · · pNΩ NΩ deﬁ where pnm is necessarily equal to zero if ag","equation_id":"Eq. (2)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"\\mathbf{P}=\\begin{pmatrix} p_{11} & \\cdots & p_{1N_\\Omega} \\\\ \\vdots & & \\vdots \\\\ p_{N_\\Omega 1} & \\cdots & p_{N_\\Omega N_\\Omega} \\end{pmatrix} (2); where p_{nm} is necessarily equal to zero if agent m is not in agent n’s trading partnership set \\omega_n. Net powers are then obtained by p_n=\\sum_{m\\in\\omega_n}p_{nm} as in (1c). As outlined in (1b), P is skew-symmetric to insure power balance of each trade, so p_{nn}=0. This allows to potentially individualize prices per trade."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e20","location":{"location_id":"src-12e1fd7a17-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"II. P2P Market Design","anchor_text":"on with (8). Finally, each agent n broadcasts its local residuals to ms all and, when all local resi","equation_id":"Eq. (6)-(8)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The overall negotiation mechanism occurs as follows. Each market participant first solves its own local optimization (6a). Once updated, each agent n individually sends its trade proposals (p_{nm}^{k+1})_{m\\in\\omega} to each partner m\\in\\omega_n. After receiving all counter proposals (p_{mn}^{k+1})_{m\\in\\omega}, agent n can compute its new trade prices (\\lambda_{nm}^{k+1})_{m\\in\\omega} with (6b), and local residuals (r_n,s_n)^{k+1} with (8). Finally, each agent n broadcasts its local residuals to all and, when all local residuals (r_i,s_i)^{k+1}_{i\\in\\Omega\\setminus\\{n\\}} are received, tests global stopping criteria (7). This process is repeated until convergence. Being decentralized the negotiation mechanism is not supported by a central entity. However, as most information exchanges, a communication standard needs to be defined by an institutional organization to associate a communication protocol between peers participating in the market."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Bilateral quantity proposals produced by the update (6a). | Buying-side quantity updates in the decentralized consensus-ADMM negotiation of (6). | Buying-side trade proposals in the decentralized P2P negotiation. | Individual buying-side bilateral proposals in the update (6a). | Requested-power updates in (6a), jointly with the agent's other bilateral proposals. | Submission of buying-side trade proposals in the decentralized P2P negotiation.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e20"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E002","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"bidding.demand","type":"limits","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e20"]},"paper_scope_note":"The bilateral negotiated price update and the exogenous network fee signal are separately limited in meaning; partner-set constraints, incentive intent, and ADMM computational dependencies cannot be transmitted in a mixed way."}});
